/*!
\page page_strpscollection StRpsCollection — Collection Documentation

\section rps_overview Overview

\ref StRpsCollection is the top-level event-level container for the
<b>Roman Pot System (RPS)</b>, used in the pp2pp experiment to detect
forward-scattered protons in elastic and diffractive p+p collisions at RHIC.

The system comprises eight Roman Pot detector stations (0–7) placed along both
RHIC beam lines.  Each station houses four silicon strip detector planes and two
PMT-based scintillator timing detectors.

The collection provides access to:
- The eight \ref StRpsRomanPot detector stations (stored by value).
- Reconstructed track points (\ref StRpsTrackPoint) — one per station.
- Reconstructed global forward proton tracks (\ref StRpsTrack).

\section rps_ownership Object Ownership

- <b>mRomanPots[8]</b>: Stored <b>by value</b> inside the collection.  Their
  silicon planes and clusters are nested objects; no separate heap allocation.
- <b>mTrackPoints</b> (\c StSPtrVecRpsTrackPoint): Owned; deleted by \c StSPtrVec.
- <b>mTracks</b> (\c StSPtrVecRpsTrack): Owned; same semantics.
- The collection destructor is a <b>no-op</b>; cleanup by \c StSPtrVec and the
  \c StEvent framework.

\section rps_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StRpsRomanPot[8] | mRomanPots | Array of eight Roman Pot stations, indexed 0–7. Each contains 4 silicon planes (\ref StRpsPlane) and 2 PMT timing detectors. |
| \c UChar_t | mSiliconBunch | Silicon detector bunch crossing number (default 0). |
| \c StSPtrVecRpsTrackPoint | mTrackPoints | Reconstructed track points (\ref StRpsTrackPoint), owned. |
| \c StSPtrVecRpsTrack | mTracks | Reconstructed forward proton tracks (\ref StRpsTrack), owned. |

\section rps_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c numberOfRomanPots() const | Always returns 8. |
| \c romanPot(unsigned int i) | Pointer to Roman Pot at index \c i (0–7); \c nullptr if out of range. |
| \c clusters() const | Flat list of all clusters from all planes of all pots (assembled on the fly). |
| \c trackPoints() const | Non-owning list of all reconstructed track points. |
| \c tracks() const | Non-owning list of all reconstructed forward proton tracks. |
| \c siliconBunch() const | Returns the silicon bunch crossing number. |
| \c setSiliconBunch(unsigned char) | Sets the silicon bunch crossing number. |
| \c addTrackPoint(const StRpsTrackPoint*) | Appends a track point. |
| \c addTrack(const StRpsTrack*) | Appends a forward proton track. |

\section rps_layout Roman Pot Layout

The eight pots are split: four on each beam side (east/west), numbered from the
IP outward.  Each pot holds:
- 4 silicon strip detector planes (accessed via \c plane(0)–\c plane(3)).
- 2 PMT scintillator timing detectors: \c adc(0/1) and \c tac(0/1).

\section rps_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StRpsCollection* rpsColl = event->rpsCollection();
if (!rpsColl) return;

for (unsigned int i = 0; i < rpsColl->numberOfRomanPots(); ++i) {
    const StRpsRomanPot* rp = rpsColl->romanPot(i);
    if (!rp) continue;
    for (unsigned int j = 0; j < rp->numberOfPlanes(); ++j) {
        const StRpsPlane* plane = rp->plane(j);
        // use plane->cluster(k) ...
    }
}

StPtrVecRpsTrack tracks = rpsColl->tracks();
for (size_t i = 0; i < tracks.size(); ++i) {
    const StRpsTrack* trk = tracks[i];
    // use trk->...
}
\endcode

\see StRpsRomanPot, StRpsPlane, StRpsTrackPoint, StRpsTrack
*/
